# A FactExternal sent back ([NCBK.10.4], [RFCS.23.4], [RFCS.23.7]). Fixture
# 127_resend.
#
# `resend K` asserts, through `assert_external`, the K-th fact this run sent
# as a call argument: each runtime reads back the bytes it wrote, which the
# `call` lines have already compared. What this compares is what each does
# with them -- every fact the record adds is an ordinary assert on the trace,
# and a refused record prints `external_refused` with its status.
#
# Handles: 0 the Ref, 1 the Seed, 2 N0, 3-6 the triggers, 7 the Ref replaced.
# @spec [RFCS.24.1]
assert Ref id="a" note="x"
assert Seed k=1
assert N0 n=0
pump
# The four calls, in rule order: sent fact 0 is the Main, 1 the Pair, 2 N16,
# 3 N17.
assert SendMain n=1
assert SendPair n=1
assert SendN16 n=1
assert SendN17 n=1
pump
#
# 1. SENT BACK WHILE LIVE. Every nested copy is equal to the live fact it was
# made from (RFCS.23.7 step 1), and the record's own fact is a no-op
# reassertion: nothing on the trace. A runtime that did not resolve the copy
# to the live fact would meet the key taken and refuse with -220.
resend 0
resend 1
resend 2
#
# 2. TOO DEEP. N17's record inlines N0 at depth 17; RFCS.23.4 admits 16, so
# it is DS_ERR_PARSE (-100) whatever is live.
resend 3
#
# 3. THE KEY TAKEN. The Ref is replaced with another note, and Main and Pair
# re-derived from the new one. The sent Main still carries the old Ref: equal
# to no live fact, and its key `a` is held, so the record is refused whole
# with DS_ERR_FACT_REF_CONFLICT (-220) and nothing is asserted.
assert Ref id="a" note="y"
pump
resend 0
#
# 4. ONE FACT INLINED TWICE, NOTHING LIVE. With the Ref retracted, Main and
# Pair go with it. The sent Pair carries the old Ref in both slots: the first
# copy is asserted (step 2), the second is equal to it and is the same fact,
# so one Ref and one Pair arrive.
retract 7
pump
resend 1
pump
#
# 5. A CHAIN OF SEVENTEEN, ASSERTED. With N0 retracted the chain goes. The
# sent N16 inlines N15 .. N0, none live: all seventeen arrive, the deepest
# first, and the pump after re-derives N17 from the N16 that came back.
retract 2
pump
resend 2
pump
